  "new_v0_6_claims": [
    "affine substitution by a nonzero complex slope preserves the degree-d bounded polynomial subspace and gives a linear equivalence",
    "the width support {k in ZMod T | g divides k.val} is explicitly equivalent to Fin(T/g) and therefore has cardinality T/g",
    "the degree-d bounded polynomial fiber has finrank d+1 and its ZMod T profile space has finrank T(d+1)",
    "the bounded Fourier width projector has range finrank (T/g)(d+1)",
    "the DFT-conjugated bounded Reynolds projector has the same exact range finrank",
    "for any projector P and linear equivalence U, the saved normal form P o U has exactly Range(P)",
    "for positive m, the bounded projector-factorized affine section normal form has rank (T/gcd(T,m))(d+1)",
    "its nullity is (T-T/gcd(T,m))(d+1)",
    "over any field of characteristic p, if p divides m then affine substitution X -> mX+r collapses every polynomial to the constant f(r)",
    "over any field of characteristic p, if p does not divide m then the radix scalar m is nonzero"
  ],
  "explicit_boundaries": [
    "Bell generalized Cobham theorem remains external and is not formalized",
    "the rank/nullity law is proved for the finite complex degree-bounded projector-factorized affine section normal form",
    "v0.6.0 does not identify that saved normal form with any stronger unsaved root-aggregation section operator",
    "the generic positive-characteristic theorem isolates affine collapse but does not constitute a full DFT/Reynolds rank theorem over arbitrary coefficient fields",
    "the naive base-independent integral normal form remains false and is not revived",
    "positive radices are assumed in the raw-radix and rank/nullity laws",
    "Lean verification does not establish literature novelty or priority"
  ],
  "external_inputs": [
    {
      "name": "Bell generalized Cobham theorem",
      "status": "external / not formalized",
      "use_boundary": "may only enter downstream through an explicit conclusion interface"
    }
  ],
